---
const mistakes = [
  "Ordering a quality of earnings report before the seller has agreed on terms. $8,000 to $15,000, and the deal dies in week two.",
  "Paying an M&A attorney to draft an LOI when a standard template would have done the job. $2,000 to $4,000.",
  "Running the QoE and the legal review at the same time instead of QoE first. The deal dies on the numbers after the attorney has billed $6,000.",
  "Picking a lender who was never going to do the deal, finding out in month three, and starting over.",
  "Skipping a $500 lien or environmental search and paying for it at closing.",
  "Overpaying by half a turn on the multiple because nobody told you what the business would actually trade for. On a $1.5M deal, that's $75,000.",
];
---

<section class="py-16 md:py-24">
  <div class="fade-in-section mx-auto max-w-[1100px] px-4 sm:px-6">
    <h2
      class="max-w-3xl font-serif text-3xl font-semibold leading-tight tracking-tight sm:text-4xl"
    >
      Most first-time buyers don't lose money on the price. They lose it on the
      order of operations.
    </h2>
    <p class="mt-4 text-lg text-ink-soft">
      These are things I see regularly. All of them are avoidable.
    </p>

    <ul class="mt-10 flex max-w-[46rem] flex-col divide-y divide-line">
      {
        mistakes.map((mistake) => (
          <li class="py-5 leading-relaxed text-ink">{mistake}</li>
        ))
      }
    </ul>

    <p class="mt-10 max-w-prose text-lg leading-relaxed text-ink-soft">
      Your CPA, your attorney, the QoE firm, and your lender are all necessary
      and they all cost real money. None of them is paid to tell you when to
      bring in the next one, or when to stop. That's what I do. The right
      people, in the right order, and a clear read on whether the deal is worth
      spending on before the expensive part starts.
    </p>

    <div class="mt-12 max-w-md border-l-2 border-accent bg-white/60 py-6 pl-6 pr-6">
      <p class="text-base text-ink">Six months of Quarterback: $3,000</p>
      <p class="mt-2 text-base text-ink">Under Contract: $2,500</p>
      <p class="mt-2 text-base text-ink">
        One QoE report on a deal that was going to die anyway: $10,000
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
